{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat README.md; command -v codex; ls -l \"$(command -v codex)\"; rg -n '\"'codex|sandbox|HOME' . --glob '\"'!runs/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n/opt/homebrew/bin/codex\nlrwxr-xr-x  1 valentinakoniukhova  admin  46 Oct  3 09:46 /opt/homebrew/bin/codex -> ../lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/bin/codex.js\n./sandbox/agent.sb:2:;; unreachable. Only the agent's own install is opened. Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D HOME=<real home>.\n./sandbox/agent.sb:5:(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n./sandbox/agent.sb:6:(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n./sandbox/agent.sb:7:(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n./sandbox/agent.sb:8:(allow file-write* (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n./run.sh:3:# lanes: codex   Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n./run.sh:4:#        kimi    Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n./run.sh:13:codex_run() {\n./run.sh:14:  ( cd \"$W\" && timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json \\\n./run.sh:18:# Kimi's output goes to Moonshot: its shell runs under sandbox/agent.sb with an empty scratch HOME.\n./run.sh:20:  local REAL=\"$HOME\" SH; SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/khome-XXXXXX)\n./run.sh:21:  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$SH\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n./run.sh:22:      env KIMI_CODE_HOME=\"$REAL/.kimi-code\" timeout $TO \"$REAL/.kimi-code/bin/kimi\" -p \"$P\" --output-format stream-json \\\n./run.sh:29:  codex) codex_run;;\n./README.md:19:- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n./README.md:21:  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n./README.md:22:  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
